From 70b70c998e3703f9c6cebefad5f8e967e2dc1dee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:33:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] test(motion): fold the motion integration tests into domain
 directory suites

The 153 flat, non-slow test files of crates/motion/tests move into ten
directory suites: adaptive2d, contour2d, machining2d, holes, entry_links,
machining3d, finishing3d, multiaxis, turning and edges_edm. Each suite
root declares one module for each former file. The slow binaries
finish3d, pivot5d and flow stay flat, and rest_adaptive and rotary_flow
stay as they were. camcraft-motion now has 15 test binaries, not 158.

The files move with git mv. Only path-relative lines change: the shared
common and adaptive_troch helpers are declared once in the suite root,
and three #[path]/include_str! lines get a ../ prefix. The Gate map
paragraphs stay in the modules; the gate reads them through the root.

The test count stays at 2014 (78 ignored). xtask pins the fold
(motion_tests_fold_into_at_most_sixteen_binaries); two live-tree xtask
tests now name the suites that hold arcs and cross_invariance.

Fixes #3189

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
